     "text": "GPU: Optimize Throughput of a Large Number of Simple Threads\n  Example: Executing Thread Blocks\n\n¡ A thread block is assigned to one SM\n\n   ¡ Up to 8 blocks to each SM\n\n   ¡  Fermi SM can take up to 1536 threads\n     ¡ Could be 256 * 6 blocks\n\n     ¡  Or 512 * 3 blocks, etc.\n\n\n\n   ¡  Each block is divided into 32-thread warps\n\n      ¡  Scheduling by the warp scheduler within a SM.\n\n   ¡  Single Instruction, Multiple Threads (SIMT)\n       abstraction\n\n      ¡  Threads in a wrap should execution same\n           codes/instructions.\n\n      ¡  However, thread is allowed to execute different\n          branches.",
